  https://github.com/Adolanium/hermes-rss) (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's two halves, from public/prompt-enhance/desktop/plugin.js.
Its enhancer set (Clarify, Tighten, Grammar, Expand, Summarize) and their
instruction texts, the payload that puts a saved prompt and the current draft
together under "Context:", the library of folders, names and bodies seeded with
those five, saving, listing, showing and deleting a prompt, and the one-shot
rewrite: an enhancer's instruction plus "Return only the rewritten prompt. No
preamble and no code fence.", the draft as the input, and only the rewritten
prompt back. The rewrite is one POST to an OpenAI-compatible
chat/completions endpoint named in the config section, where the original asked
the host for its one-shot call; the library is one JSON file under the home
instead of the plugin host's storage.

Left out: everything that exists only because the original draws into the Hermes
desktop composer -- the composer icon and its spinner, the dropdown menus, the
glyphs (Codicon names), the drag-and-drop reorder, the edit dialogs, the CSS
that reached into the host's dialog markup, and the per-session undo of an
enhancement. Also left out: the one-call model override, which ran the host's
/model command with --once for the session it was in; a cell has no session
model to override, and the section's model is the rewrite's model. Nothing of
the original's own code is bundled; it is all reimplemented in Common Lisp
against Nodecode's cell contract.

LICENSE in this folder is that repository's LICENSE file, unchanged.
